ntly unique per environment, like database record keys."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unique for the lifetime of a process, like global incrementing integers."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unique for the lifetime of an object, like object identifiers."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unique within the current collection, like collection indices."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s up to both the conformer and the receiver of the protocol to document"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the nature of the identity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Conforming to the Identifiable Protocol","anchor":"Conforming-to-the-Identifiable-Protocol","level":1,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable"},{"type":"text","text":" provides a default implementation for class types (using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObjectIdentifier"},{"type":"text","text":"), which is only guaranteed to remain unique for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lifetime of an object. If an object has a stronger notion of identity, it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"may be appropriate to provide a custom implementation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Equality and Ordering","generated":true,"anchor":"Equality-and-Ordering","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Equatable","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Comparable"]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/identifiable"]}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Identifiable":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A class of types whose instances hold the value of an entity with stable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"t